=Write ONLY the opening paragraph of a horror short story. 50 to 70 words. Nothing more.

CREATIVE BRIEF:
{{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisionsText }}

BEAT 1 OF YOUR OUTLINE TO USE AS BASIS:
{{ $json.output[0].content[0].text }}

REQUIREMENTS:
- POV must be: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.pov }}
- Opening style: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.opening_style }}
- Tone: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.tone_modifier }}
- Setting: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.setting }}
- Hint at the wrongness without naming it
- Do not introduce any character by name yet unless the opening style demands it
- The final sentence of this paragraph must create a reason to keep reading

Do not write a title. Do not continue past the first paragraph. Output only the paragraph.

=Write a complete horror short story of 300–350 words.

CREATIVE BRIEF:
{{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisionsText }}

STORY OUTLINE — follow this structure beat by beat:
{{ $('Node 1').item.json.output[0].content[0].text }}

BEGIN WITH THIS EXACT OPENING PARAGRAPH — reproduce it word for word, then continue:
{{ $json.output[0].content[0].text }}

WRITING RULES:
- POV throughout: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.pov }}
- Horror mode: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.horror_mode }}
- Tone: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.tone_modifier }}
- Constraint to follow: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.narrative_constraint }}
- Source of wrongness: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.source_of_wrongness }} — this must be present from the first third but never named directly
- The ending must SHOW the consequence of: {{ $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions.ending_type }} — through action or image, not explanation
- Plant at least 2 foreshadowing details in the first third that pay off in the final third
- The threat or wrongness must never be fully described — imply, suggest, show edges
- In scenes of rising tension use short sentences. In scenes of dread or waiting use long ones
- No comedy. No warmth that resolves. No overt explanation of what the reader should feel
- No title. Output only the story.
- IMPORTANT: Stop writing before the final paragraph. 
Write everything up to but not including the ending. 
End your output mid-story at the moment just before 
the final consequence lands. Do not resolve anything.

